Ruinux kernel
=============

The Ruinux kernel is a completely independent fork of the Linux kernel. Ruinux is distinct from Linux in two ways:
- Instead of being controlled by Linus Torvalds and a thriving developer comumunity, Ruinux is controlled by centuryglass (Anthony Brown), a solo developer who isn't particularly noteworthy.
- While Linux is an actively maintained project that's constantly updating and improving, Ruinux promises to instead never update or improve.

Q and A
=======

Q: Why?

A: Why not?  Forks are free.

Q: When should I use Ruinux?

A: Only when it's funny. Make sure to evaluate this carefully, because in almost all cases where one might suspect Ruinux would be funny, it is actually just obnoxious.

Q: Do you use Ruinux?

A: No.
